VALUES (662, '0', $t$ASK 662: the Holy Ghost is the Spirit of God (ruach, pneuma): sight 1824, corrections to sights 1407 and 1345, and sights 1825 to 1828 from the four readings$t$,
  $t$The operator asked on 2026-11-25 (18:49 CST) for a deep dive on the Holy Ghost as ruach and pneuma, then (19:23 CST) for a standalone sight, taught it part by part from 20:19 CST, and on 21:34 CST ordered a complete detailed sight with updates to others if needed; at 21:40 CST he ruled it goes in before the run, the point being an improved run. At 21:38 and 23:29 CST he gave leave for deep dives on the interests that arose, and at 00:07 CST 2026-11-26, having been given four W1-passed readings, he wrote: add them to the corpus. Change: one new sight on the Spirit (1824); two small corrections to sights 1407 and 1345; four new sights from the readings (1825 born of the Spirit, 1826 the promised sons, 1827 Christ means anointed, 1828 gennao at every row). Expected effect: on the phrase of the Holy Ghost at Matthew 1:18 and 1:20 the Oracle is served the rows and adds supporting evidence instead of repeating (ASK 659 held for one clean run first). Not changed: any guard, any conclusion, the engine, any manual, Sight 10 (its absence-form line waits for the operator's word).$t$,
  'in part',
  $t$WRITTEN AND READ BACK: all seven rows by W1 (Wall 12326, 12334, 12341, 12365). Sight 1824 is embedded (Wall 12339). IN PART because: no run since the writes; sights 1825 to 1828 had no embedding at the write (hourly workflow; W4 to confirm); sights 1407 and 1345 keep old vectors until after the next run (card press After your next run, Wall 12343); part (14) of sight 1824 is still marked open in its stored text though sight 1825 now reads it. MISTAKES, W3: (1) the three writes of 2026-11-25 (sight 1824 insert, its notes correction, the 1407 and 1345 updates) carried no audit row in their calls; found 00:21 CST 2026-11-26 and entered late as audit 42583, 42584, 42585. (2) Sight 1824 notes were filed with counts not rerun (24 and 23); corrected to 23 and 25 on a card (Wall 12329 to 12334). (3) The first title of sight 1826 said nine sons were announced; eight were, and Samuel was asked for (W1 F1, Wall 12361). (4) The first other-sights search was case-sensitive and missed four sights (Wall 12337). (5) Two typed times ran ahead of the clock (Wall 12335, 12364). MISTAKE, W1: its first counts on Wall 12326 were wrong for a missing coalesce (Wall 12330). NOT CHECKED by W3: retrieval of any of the rows by the Oracle; W1 did not read the audit rows.$t$,
  '12282, 12288, 12294, 12320, 12321, 12322, 12323, 12324, 12326, 12328, 12329, 12330, 12333, 12334, 12335, 12336, 12337, 12338, 12339, 12340, 12341, 12342, 12343, 12360, 12361, 12362, 12363, 12364, 12365',
  current_setting('truth.session_id'), NULL,
  to_jsonb($t$In the W3 thread, verbatim. 21:34 CST 2026-11-25: "yes, make a complete detailed sight ... update others if needed .. that was a very nice exchange.  From a human perspective it was amazing". 21:38 CST: "please feel free to do any deep drives on additional interests that arose." 23:29 CST: "Do you have anything else you'd like to continue to deep dive on?" 00:07 CST 2026-11-26: "add them to the corpus". Relayed by the coordinator at 21:40 CST 2026-11-25 (not read by W3 in the project chat): "it shouldn't be ... the point is to have an improved run ... with improved results".$t$::text),
  $j${"answer": "Write it now; Correct the notes; Make both; After your next run; Write the four sights now", "question": "five cards in the W3 thread, one per write or deferral", "thread": "W3", "press_times": {"Write it now (sight 1824)": "21:40 CST 2026-11-25", "Correct the notes (sight 1824 notes)": "21:46 CST 2026-11-25", "Make both (sights 1407, 1345)": "22:17 CST 2026-11-25", "After your next run (vectors of 1407, 1345)": "22:22 CST 2026-11-25", "Write the four sights now (1825 to 1828)": "00:15 CST 2026-11-26"}, "card_id_last": "cmsg_017ZQamDMHrS6fqMHnQDVo58XBda6ucNu88pNYNBHCfV9j", "source": "W3's own thread; press times as posted on Wall 12324, 12333, 12340, 12343, 12363"}$j$::jsonb,
  'W3',
  $j${"md5": null, "path": null, "note": "no plan file: doctrine work is undefined work and stays on the Wall (Wall manual section 2). Each text was posted for W1's grade before its card.", "source": "Wall 12320 to 12323, 12335 to 12338, 12360 to 12362"}$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[{"path": "ask662/w3/sight_holy_ghost_draft5.md", "md5": "a6c0da82fdae4279f1c46183bbc3f915", "what": "graded text of sight 1824"}, {"path": "ask662/w3/other_sights_update_list.md", "md5": "27a3d726b0f1c883f32e12302c876297", "what": "the other Holy Ghost sights read; source of the 1407 and 1345 changes"}, {"path": "ask662/w3/sights4/sight_draft_1.md", "md5": "93f8814e3e96ab9c8292ce8daa09430f", "what": "sight 1825 draft"}, {"path": "ask662/w3/sights4/sight_draft_2.md", "md5": "f88e85aad027dd87243c3785ab16874f", "what": "sight 1826 draft (rev 2 with W1's optional notes wording)"}, {"path": "ask662/w3/sights4/sight_draft_3.md", "md5": "7a1a9061477039cd72383a0bba56df42", "what": "sight 1827 draft"}, {"path": "ask662/w3/sights4/sight_draft_4.md", "md5": "e75070c5b305800a8097a46a9deef491", "what": "sight 1828 draft"}, {"path": "ask662/w3/sights4/build4.py", "md5": "ab4b08184c38d27f884f8b19e1d36f17", "what": "builds each draft from its graded reading by asserted replacements"}]$j$::jsonb,
